Z||000005||Formula88||12-07-2001||10:28 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Phil:<BR><B>I just finished up #10. Takes my puter about 30 hrs. per<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What processor are you running?  It takes my PIII 800 about 8-10hrs, but my old Pentium 200 took 40-50hrs each.  You can dramatically speed up it's processing by setting the screen saver to "Go to blank screen" after "0" minutes.  It uses a lot of CPU power just to draw the pretty little graphics for the screen saver.  I have mine set to go blank after 1 minute.  I used to have it set to run in the backround all the time, but I've switched it to run only when the screen saver is active now.  It would cause my games to hiccup occasionally when running in the backround. Can't have that.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>There are some people who've done insane amounts of work units!  Logging several THOUSAND years of CPU time.  Makes me wonder just how many PC's they're running it on!  I'm running mine on just my 1 home PC.  I run it occasionally on my laptop, but it only gets an extra 2 or maybe 3 work units a week, cuz it's not on all the time.||||reg||1
